<title>CANADA: MOTOR RACING-SCHUMACHER WINS CANADIAN GRAND PRIX.</title>
<headline>MOTOR RACING-SCHUMACHER WINS CANADIAN GRAND PRIX.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Michael Schumacher of Germany, driving a Ferrari, won the Canadian Grand Prix on Sunday after an accident caused the race to be halted after 56 laps.</p>
<p>Jean Alesi of France in a Benetton was second and Italian Giancarlo Fisichella of Italy in a Jordan was third, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Heinz-Harald Frentzen of Germany was fourth in a Williams, Johnny Herbert of Britain was fifth in a Sauber and Shinji Nakano of Japan in a Prost was sixth.  </p>
<p>World drivers' championship standings (after seven rounds):</p>
<p>  1. Michael Schumacher (Germany)	    37</p>
<p>  2. Jacques Villeneuve (Canada)	     30</p>
<p>  3. Olivier Panis (France)		    15</p>
<p>  4. Eddie Irvine (Britain)		    14</p>
<p>  5 equal. Heinz-Harald Frentzen (Germany) 13</p>
<p>  5 equal. Jean Alesi (France)		 13</p>
<p>  7. David Coulthard (Britain)		 11</p>
<p>  8 equal. Gerhard Berger  (Germany)	 10</p>
<p>  8 equal. Mika Hakkinen (Finland)	   10</p>
<p> 10. Giancarlo Fisichella (Italy)	     8</p>
<p> 11. Rubens Barrichello (Brazil)		6</p>
<p> 12. Johnny Herbert (Britain)		   7</p>
<p> 13. Ralf Schumacher (Germany)		  4</p>
<p> 14. Mika Salo (Finland)			  2</p>
<p> 15. Nicola Larini (Italy)			1</p>
<p> 16. Shinji Nakano (Japan)			1</p>
<p>Constructors' championship:</p>
<p>  1. Ferrari					 51 points</p>
<p>  2. Williams					43</p>
<p>  3. Benetton					23</p>
<p>  3. McLaren					 21</p>
<p>  5. Prost					   16</p>
<p>  6. Jordan					  12</p>
<p>  7. Sauber					   8</p>
<p>  8. Stewart					  6</p>
<p>  9. Tyrrell					  2</p>
